# Bounded memory

No routine workflow may accumulate an unbounded number of source items, events,
API responses, prompts, or cached objects in process memory. Paginate, stream,
batch, persist incrementally, or apply explicit resource limits. Queue and
worker concurrency must be bounded and configurable. Performance tests record
RSS and peak RSS.
